+# Batch 50 — Step 1 authoring evidence
+
+Run: `advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23`  
+Batch: 50 (`beta`, `advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry`)
+
+## Plan and design comparison
+
+The complete S4 design section in `research/plan-advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry-track.md` and the live `research/plan-spec.json` agree on the A/B IDs, title, order 1006, category, library, required pages, scope, and two planned item IDs. The design requires a source-qualified four-dimensional N=2 gauge/hyper model, sphere radius/coupling/contour, one-loop and instanton factors, and Pestun's explicit warning that the noncommutative S4 deformation is assumed rather than constructed. No plan/design conflict was found.
+
+The scaffold's original postulate had no direct item dependency and the example named only the postulate. The authored postulate adds `def-qftx-susy-background-data` as a formulation prerequisite. The example adds `def-axiom-of-choice`, `thm-adhm-fixed-point-instanton-count`, and `pthm-qftx-qexact-localization-ward-identity`, with mathematical-premise and physical-result roles, because the actual fixed-point theorem assumes full AC and the planned field-theory Ward input is relevant to the proposed localization argument. The exact current interfaces were inspected; the q-exact theorem does not match the N=2* U(2) model, so that edge remains open and the complete conditional requirement is stated in the consuming item.
+
+For the group and measure convention, this batch uses Pestun's full Lie-algebra expression from Eq. (1.4), with `1/vol(U(2))`, `exp(-8 pi^2 r^2 (a,a)/gYM^2)`, and the source's `Z1-loop(ia) |Zinst(ia)|^2`. The local research note `research-localization-bps.md` also displays a schematic Cartan rewrite with a separate Weyl factor and a slightly different normalization described there as convention-dependent. The authored item chooses the primary source's full-Lie-algebra Eq. (1.4) and keeps its Weyl factor out of the root-product determinant; it does not combine the two normalizations.
+
+## Item checkpoint — `post-qftx-s4-n2-localization-model`
+
+The Postulate adopts a round Euclidean S4 model with global group U(2), one N=2 vector multiplet, one adjoint hypermultiplet of real Euclidean mass `m_E`, the source's mass deformation, coupling/theta convention, selected conformal-Killing-spinor data and Q-square, continued contour, and explicit formal noncommutative regulator assumption. It states no constructed measure, regulator-removal limit, continuum Q-exact theorem, or empirical claim. The background definition `def-qftx-susy-background-data` is an exact formulation prerequisite and currently has a ready Step-1 record; the new item is dependency level 2 (background item level 1 plus one).
+
+Sources are Vasily Pestun, [arXiv:0712.2824](https://arxiv.org/pdf/0712.2824), full 58-page PDF, §1 equations (1.3)–(1.4) and regulator qualification, §2 equations (2.1)–(2.14), (2.24)–(2.30), and §5 equations (5.1), (5.11)–(5.12); and Vasilis Peelaers, [4d N=2 Localization lecture notes](https://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/3026/attachments/2163/2457/Peelaers-LectureNotes.pdf), complete 21-page notes, Lecture 1 §§1.1–1.2 equations (19)–(30), PDF pp. 3–5, and Lecture 2 equations (31)–(35), PDF pp. 5–6. Pestun's S4 regulator nonconstruction is retained. The Peelaers title page says the notes were not proofread; they corroborate background and formal factors but do not prove a continuum measure. Both full texts passed the current `source-fetch-check --stamp` run.
+
+## Item checkpoint — `ex-qftx-s4-n2-partition-function`
+
+The Example reports Pestun's formal U(2) matrix-integral expression and defines its one-loop and N=2* instanton factors, including the shifted mass `mtilde=m_E+(epsilon1+epsilon2)/2`. It keeps generic equivariant variables through the two-term charge-one calculation, maps the dual ADHM framing weights by `a_A=-a_P`, and specializes only after summation to `epsilon1=epsilon2=1/r` and the source's continued Nekrasov weights `a_P=i a_E`. Its proof verifies the two size-one tuples, tangent Euler factors and numerator, dimensions, and the round-sphere massless limit. The matrix formula is expressly source-reported; the continuum interpretation and pole coefficient require assumptions A1–A3.
+
+The direct mathematical suppliers are `thm-adhm-fixed-point-instanton-count` (full AC and its positive-FI partition/tangent-character interface) and `def-axiom-of-choice`. The ADHM theorem's current Step-1 record is escalated: its local fixed-point proof is complete, but its ABBV/Borel prerequisite readiness chain is unresolved, and the ADHM/monad comparisons and noncompact pushforward remain conditional. The example names these limits and does not claim the compact ABBV theorem gives a noncompact pushforward.
+
+The planned Ward interface is stated exactly as a conditional hypothesis in A1: one fixed N=2* U(2) finite regulator, Q-invariant measure and cycle, anomaly-free regularization, zero Q-exact boundary integral, and compact-parameter L1 majorants, yielding finite-parameter constancy only. The actual current `pthm-qftx-qexact-localization-ward-identity` was inspected in full. Its model is massless N=4 SU(2), so it is not the required U(2) supplier; its Step-1 readiness record is also missing. A2 separately assumes a justified large-t saddle limit and noncompact positive-FI ADHM pushforward with precise integration/support/compactification hypotheses. A3 separately assumes the pole-factor identification and the source's S4-to-R4 noncommutative regulator match. These assumptions are not claimed proved.
+
+The q1 sign and denominator match was checked directly: the ADHM theorem has dual framing character `W=sum e_alpha^{-1}`, so its additive weights `b_alpha` map to Pestun's Nekrasov weights as `b_alpha=-a_alpha^P`. The two one-box tangent Euler products then agree with the two denominators in Pestun's Eq. (5.12). Pestun's Eq. (5.12) gives the same charge-one numerator after the source mass shift. The only one-box tuples are `((Box),empty)` and `(empty,(Box))`.
+
+## Source harvest and retrieval
+
+`research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-50.coverage.json` records the full URLs, locators, actual inspected extent, limitations, supported item IDs, and a disposition for each harvested source result. The primary is Pestun's paper; the independent full lecture-note treatment is Peelaers. The source-fetch command initially received the shorthand `--coverage 50`, which correctly found no file; no retrieval was attempted on that invocation. The correct command, `node tools/physics-support/source-fetch-check.mjs --coverage research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-50.coverage.json --stamp`, completed successfully: 2/2 full-text sources fetch-verified, both newly stamped, 0 source drops. No retrieval failed, so `source_resolution` is empty in the coverage and companion source-resolution record; no recovery retry or alternative proof was needed.
+
+## Page and dependency levels
+
+The A page keeps all three planned page prerequisites. The current q-exact page's only Ward theorem is N=4 SU(2)-specific; the ADHM page's local fixed-point interface is relevant but its current readiness is escalated and the noncompact pushforward is absent; the current supersymmetric moduli/duality page develops pure SU(2) N=2 data and has no N=2* U(2) interface. Those exact page edges remain `open`. The A-to-B edge is within this batch and is not entered in the cross-batch file.
+
+The run-wide page level for batch 50 is 7; its planned page suppliers are batches 12 (level 3), 33 (level 6), and 48 (level 6). Item levels are recomputed separately from in-run item dependencies: Postulate level 2; Example level 10, one above its maximum in-run supplier level 9 (the current q-exact theorem). The out-of-run full-AC definition does not raise the item level. No dependency cycle was found in the authored pair.
+
+`research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-50.cross-batch-dependencies.json` has one row per exact cross-batch page/item edge. `verified` is limited to the background-definition interface; the three page edges and both unresolved item suppliers are `open`. No transitive observations were added as review rows.
+
+## Contracts, validation and readiness
+
+The A/B library pages contain YAML frontmatter only and no Markdown summary body. The manifest now contains the two complete item records and their uninterrupted statements. The proof contract maps all six numbered example steps, exact current supplier excerpts, each stated fact/hypothesis, boundary cases, and the finite one-box and massless-limit checks; the Postulate has its required physics-review worksheet.
+
+Scoped check outcomes and final Step-1 records will be appended here after the final item/manifest synchronization and validation pass. The current known readiness dispositions are: Postulate may be recorded `ready` after its current prerequisite and contract checks; Example must be `escalated` unless the N=2* U(2) Ward interface, ADHM readiness chain, and required noncompact/pole inputs are supplied. No existing escalation will be overwritten and no owner flag will be used.
+
+Next action: synchronize the final item statements into the batch manifest; run scoped source, coverage, dependency, proof-contract, content-policy, precheck, render, and proof-layout checks; repair in-scope defects; then record each Step-1 decision with exact dependency evidence.

