+## Facts & Assumptions
+
+**Given:** The adopted Euclidean $\mathcal N=2^*$ $U(2)$ model, its round $S^4_r$ source contour, its dimensionless instanton parameter, and the formal source formula above. For the fixed-point calculation assume full AC, positive ADHM stability $\zeta>0$, and algebraically independent generic equivariant variables; specialize only after summing the rational terms.
+
+[F1] [[post-qftx-s4-n2-localization-model]]: the physical model is $U(2)$ with one adjoint hypermultiplet of Euclidean mass $m_E$, the source coupling and contour, $\epsilon_1=\epsilon_2=r^{-1}$, $q=e^{2\pi i\tau}$, and an assumed but unconstructed supersymmetric noncommutative $S^4$ regulator matching Nekrasov's regulator near both poles.
+
+[F2] [[thm-adhm-fixed-point-instanton-count]]: for the positive-FI framed $U(N)$ ADHM quotient with the stated $T^2\times T_G$ action and dual-framing characters, the fixed points are $N$-tuples of partitions and their tangent characters determine inverse-Euler fixed-point weights. Its Statement assumes full AC. The inspected proof derives the fixed-point classification and tangent character locally; the ADHM/monad comparisons and any noncompact pushforward remain explicit conditional inputs.
+
+[F3] [[def-axiom-of-choice]]: full AC means every family of nonempty sets indexed by an arbitrary set has a choice function. It is carried here only because the actual ADHM theorem Statement assumes it; the one-box algebra uses finite sets.
+
+[A1] The planned Ward-identity input for this $\mathcal N=2^*$ $U(2)$ model is conditional on a fixed finite-dimensional regulator whose measure and cycle are $Q$-invariant, whose regularization is anomaly-free, whose integrand and parameter derivative satisfy the stated compact-parameter $L^1$ majorant, and whose $Q$-exact boundary integral vanishes. It would imply finite-parameter constancy only. The current carrier [[pthm-qftx-qexact-localization-ward-identity]] instead assumes the massless $\mathcal N=4$ $SU(2)$ model, so it does not supply this interface for the present model.
+
+[A2] Assume a separately justified $t\to\infty$ saddle limit for the regulator in [A1], with the convergence and sector hypotheses needed to identify its value with a noncompact equivariant pushforward on the positive-FI $U(2)$ ADHM quotient whose fixed-point sum uses the inverse tangent Euler classes in [F2]. The integration, support, and compactification hypotheses must be supplied; neither compact ABBV nor the local fixed-point calculation in [F2] supplies them.
+
+[A3] Assume a $T$-equivariant identification of the positive-FI ADHM fixed-point series with Pestun's Nekrasov pole factor, using the mass shift and framing-sign convention stated in the Example. The source's supersymmetry-compatible noncommutative deformation on $S^4$ and its agreement with the Nekrasov $\mathbb R^4$ regulator near each pole remain adopted assumptions, not constructions. No field-space measure or regulator-removal proof is used here.
+
+## Verification
+
+**Given:** [F1]–[F3] and the explicit conditional assumptions [A1]–[A3]. The equation for $Z_{S^4}^{\mathrm{formal}}$ is source-reported in [F1]; this verification does not claim to derive it from a continuum measure.
+
+1.1 For $k=1$ and $N=2$, the only partition pairs are $((\Box),\varnothing)$ and $(\varnothing,(\Box))$. Substituting their characters into [F2] gives the tangent characters $t_1+t_2+e_2/e_1+t_1t_2e_1/e_2$ and $t_1+t_2+e_1/e_2+t_1t_2e_2/e_1$, respectively. Their ADHM-convention weights have Euler products
+$$E_1^{\mathrm A}=\epsilon_1\epsilon_2(b_2-b_1)(\epsilon_1+\epsilon_2+b_1-b_2),\qquad E_2^{\mathrm A}=\epsilon_1\epsilon_2(b_1-b_2)(\epsilon_1+\epsilon_2+b_2-b_1),$$
+where $b_\alpha=a_\alpha^{\mathrm A}=c_1^T(e_\alpha)$. Substituting $b_\alpha=-a_\alpha^{\mathrm P}$ gives $E_1^{\mathrm A}=\epsilon_1\epsilon_2(a_2^{\mathrm P}-a_1^{\mathrm P}+\epsilon_1+\epsilon_2)(a_1^{\mathrm P}-a_2^{\mathrm P})$ and $E_2^{\mathrm A}=\epsilon_1\epsilon_2(a_1^{\mathrm P}-a_2^{\mathrm P}+\epsilon_1+\epsilon_2)(a_2^{\mathrm P}-a_1^{\mathrm P})$, exactly the two source denominators in $C_1$. [given, F2, F3, algebra]
+
+2.1 For the first one-box tuple, the contributing weights in the displayed Nekrasov factor are $E_{11}=\epsilon_2$ and $E_{12}=a_2^{\mathrm P}-a_1^{\mathrm P}+\epsilon_1+\epsilon_2$. Thus its hypermultiplet numerator is $(\epsilon_1-\widetilde m)(\epsilon_2-\widetilde m)(a_2^{\mathrm P}-a_1^{\mathrm P}+\epsilon_1+\epsilon_2-\widetilde m)(a_1^{\mathrm P}-a_2^{\mathrm P}-\widetilde m)$, and its vector denominator is $E_1^{\mathrm A}$ from step 1.1. For the second color the two Coulomb weights interchange and the denominator is $E_2^{\mathrm A}$. Adding these two fixed-point contributions gives exactly $C_1$ in the Example. This is a finite formal coefficient calculation, not an integration over the noncompact quotient. [given, F2, step 1.1, algebra]
+
+2.2 The exponent in the Lie-algebra integral is dimensionless because $[r]=\mathrm{mass}^{-1}$, $[a]=\mathrm{mass}$, and $g_{\mathrm{YM}}$ is dimensionless. The one-loop product uses only ratios of mass-squared terms; each N=2* instanton numerator and denominator has the same mass degree, and $q$ is dimensionless. The Haar-volume and matrix-measure normalization remains the source's stated convention. [given, F1, step 1.1, algebra]
+
+3.1 Under [A1]–[A3], the formal coefficient is identified with the charge-one contribution at each source pole. First add the generic fixed-point terms, then specialize to $\epsilon_1=\epsilon_2=r^{-1}$, $\widetilde m=m_E+r^{-1}$, and $a_\alpha^{\mathrm P}=i a_\alpha^E$; this is Pestun's round-sphere N=2* convention. The south-pole anti-instanton uses $\bar q$ and the conjugate continued parameters. On the physical real slice this is the product represented by $|Z_{\mathrm{inst}}|^2$. Without these assumptions, only the formal ADHM coefficient in step 2.1 has been established locally; the full $S^4$ expression itself remains source-reported. [given, A1, A2, A3, F1, step 2.1]
+
+3.2 At $m_E=0$, one has $\widetilde m=(\epsilon_1+\epsilon_2)/2$; for the round-sphere specialization $\epsilon_1=\epsilon_2$, the charge-one numerator vanishes. This agrees with the source's $\mathcal N=4$ limit and does not assert a separate result for a non-round $\Omega$ background. [given, F1, step 2.1, algebra]
+
+4.1 The current Ward carrier named in [A1] has a massless $\mathcal N=4$ $SU(2)$ finite-regulator scope, so it cannot supply the planned $\mathcal N=2^*$ $U(2)$ input. Even [A1] would give only finite-$t$ constancy; the large-$t$ saddle and noncompact pushforward [A2] and the pole and regulator matching [A3] remain additional assumptions. Thus the matrix expression remains the source-reported formal example stated above, not a theorem asserting existence of a continuum $U(2)$ theory. [given, A1, A2, A3, step 3.1] ∎
