+- `coverage-checklist.mjs --require-destination`: 1 A page, 6 harvested results, 0 errors, 0 warnings. `source-fetch-check.mjs` check: 2/2 fetch-verified, 0 drops; the preceding `--stamp` fetched and stamped both full texts.
+- The scoped manifest consistency check matched both statements, dependency lists and declared levels; both library page files are frontmatter-only; all 6 cross-batch rows have valid shape and unique edges.
+- The run-wide `item-dependency-levels.mjs check` reports 22 errors elsewhere in the active run, with no error for either batch-50 item. The unrelated empty inventories are `qftx-s3-partition-functions`, `qftx-s3-partition-functions-examples`, `qftx-spectral-networks`, `qftx-spectral-networks-examples`, `qftx-adhm-zero-fi-asd-correspondence`, and `qftx-adhm-zero-fi-asd-correspondence-examples`. The other mismatched-level items are `lem-aqft-local-counterterm-shift-is-relative-coboundary`, `def-aqft-thooft-anomaly`, `def-aqft-anomaly-matching-data`, `pthm-aqft-selected-chiral-spectrum-anomaly-cancellation`, `ex-aqft-single-chiral-fundamental-polynomial`, `ex-aqft-mixed-background-counterterm-shift`, `ex-aqft-vectorlike-conjugate-chiral-pair`, `pthm-aqft-symmetry-preserving-rg-anomaly-match`, `op-aqft-fusion-two-category-anomaly-classification`, `ex-aqft-local-anomaly-counterterm-transport`, `ex-aqft-explicit-breaking-endpoint`, `lem-qftx-parametric-gauge-smoothing`, `lem-qftx-sphere-gauge-evaluation-fibration`, `lem-qftx-based-gauge-sphere-homotopy`, `thm-qftx-reduced-gauge-group-sphere-nontriviality`, and `ex-qftx-sphere-gauge-s3-components`.
+- `proof-contract-coverage.mjs` stops on the unrelated empty frontier page inventory `qftx-s3-partition-functions`; the strict batch-50 proof contract itself passes.
+- `batch-dependency-levels.mjs check` reports stale shared scheduling metadata because the postulate adds the real batch-47 item edge. The live graph retains level 7; the owner must refresh the shared schedule file.
+
+Final Step-1 records are `research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-step1-post-qftx-s4-n2-localization-model.json` (`ready`) and `research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-step1-ex-qftx-s4-n2-partition-function.json` (`escalated`). The Postulate uses the current ready `def-qftx-susy-background-data` interface. The Example is escalated because the ready q-exact supplier has the wrong model, the current ADHM theorem readiness is escalated, and A2/A3 require absent noncompact-pushforward and pole/regulator-match inputs. The records were written without `--owner`; the existing ADHM escalation was not changed.
+
